  "note": "Evidence for CKM_PQCTODAY_ECDSA_EXPLICIT_K (vendor, both engines). ACVP ECDSA SigGen is random-k, so (r, s) is reproducible only when k is an input - which is what this mechanism takes. Independent oracle: every (r, s) here was recomputed from (d, k, digest) by a standalone pure-Python affine-coordinate signer (FIPS 186-5 \u00a76.4.1, bits2int truncation) before the file was written, 40/40 matching; the engines are then checked against these upstream values, not against each other.",
  "selection": "Groups for (P-256,SHA2-256), (P-384,SHA2-384), (P-521,SHA2-512) and (P-256,SHA2-512) - the last exercises leftmost-bits truncation of a digest longer than the order. Excluded: SP800-106 randomized-hash groups and componentTest groups. Fields d, qx, qy, message are verbatim; k, r, s verbatim apart from the padding in \"encoding\"; digest is added (hashAlg over message).",
  "encoding": "k, r and s are left-padded with zero bytes to the order's byte length (orderBytes). NIST's file omits a leading zero byte on some P-521 values (5 of the 10 P-521 k's are 65 bytes); the integer values are unchanged, and CKM_PQCTODAY_ECDSA_EXPLICIT_K takes k at exactly the order's length.",
  "verification": "Every (r, s) was recomputed from (d, k, digest) by an independent pure-Python affine-coordinate signer before this file was written; all matched."
 },
